# Buzz's screens on the setup page brought up to Buzz 1.0.5, the current stable release, for the page's next image
# (1.1.0, not published). On an Apple Silicon Mac, no umbrelOS, no cost. The page from this checkout. The mocked
# suites, the browser test and the previews on ports 8831 to 8839 only (security.py and cloudflare.py each bind a port
# the system picks, as before). Not run: up.sh, check.py, Umbrel's linter and the screenshots.
# Times are UTC: on this Mac it was 2026-11-17, 19:41 PST.

# The source: block/buzz-app at v1.0.0 and v1.0.5 (a local clone, read-only git), compared for every screen the page
# draws or names. Two changes, both since 1.0.1:
# 1. Membership (block/buzz-app#3147, src/bundled/moderation/CommunityAdmin.tsx): 1.0.0 had Refresh and Invite members
#    over a boxed member list, and Invite members opened Add or invite people: the link with Copy link, Expires after,
#    Max uses and a QR code, then Add directly by public ID. 1.0.5 has a Members and an Invite tab (Tabs, variant
#    panel: text, a bar under the open one). Members: the search, Members · 1, each row with its role at the end, and
#    Retry only after a failed read. Invite: the link's QR code, beside it the link with Copy link, then Expires after
#    (3 days) and Max uses (No limit) in one box; on a Mac, Share over the code on hover (not drawn). Add directly is a
#    third tab, switched off (DIRECT_MEMBER_ADD_ENABLED = false in src/bundled/moderation/features.ts).
# 2. A new install turns on Bestie (d5288ace, block/buzz-app#2804, src/bundled/index.ts), and the dock puts it first
#    (dockOrder in src/app/shell/presentation.ts). With no community open it shows the default page icon, a browser
#    window. An install updated from 1.0.0 keeps it off.
# The same in 1.0.5: the community button and its menu (Personal space, Join a community, Create community; a dot now
# marks unread in other communities), the join dialog (Community URL, Continue twice, Publish profile & open), the
# full-page Join a community (Invite link or community URL, Join), Settings' order (settings-sections.ts unchanged;
# Plugins can now list a Claude card, past the drawings' fade), Identity and the Buzz ID card, the profile menu, Open
# Settings on Mod+,, Other options then Sign in with Builderlab or Use an existing key, which takes nsec1 only
# (key-import.ts unchanged), pairing under Mobile app or Pair mobile (PairingSettings.tsx and MobileApp.tsx unchanged),
# Moderation (relay-staff unchanged) and its messages under Manage plugins (accessMessage unchanged), buzz://connect
# (docs/deep-links.md only adds buzz://dm/new), the agent avatar packs, and an invite link's defaults and limits.
# The phone's screens aren't in buzz-app: they're the mobile app in block/buzz (mobile/). Scan a QR code, or sign in
# with email, Enter a community link, Add Community, Use Face ID, Use Touch ID, Use biometrics and Skip are the same at
# mobile-v1.0.0-rc.3, mobile-v1.1.0-rc.3 and main on 2026-11-13 (a local clone, not fetched again).

# What changed on the page:
# - The invite step's two drawings, redrawn as Membership's tabs: Members open with the Invite tab to choose, then the
#   Invite tab open with Copy link to choose. The 1.0.0 dialog's rules are gone from the stylesheet.
# - The dock in the drawings of Buzz's window (the join step's two, and Open Settings under Where to find your public
#   ID): Bestie's tile first, then Messages and Agents.
# - The invite step's captions, as given:
#   "In Buzz, open Settings. Under Community admin, choose Membership, then Invite members, or the Invite tab in newer
#   versions of Buzz."
#   -> "In Buzz, open Settings. Under Community admin, choose Membership, then the Invite tab."
#   "Copy the link and send it. Anyone with the link can join until it expires or runs out of uses. To invite one
#   person, set Max uses to 1 use first. In Buzz 1.0.0 you can also paste someone's public ID under Add directly and
#   choose Add member, then send them the address."
#   -> "Choose Copy link and send it. Anyone with the link can join until it expires or runs out of uses. To invite one
#   person, set Max uses to 1 use first."
# - Two texts that had members added by public ID:
#   The owner step: "As the owner, you add the other members and choose admins in Buzz."
#   -> "As the owner, you invite the other members and choose admins in Buzz."
#   The private network's next steps: "... or share the buzz machine with them, then add them in Buzz."
#   -> "... or share the buzz machine with them, then send them an invite link from Buzz."
# - Comments cite v1.0.5 wherever they cited 1.0.0, and the phone's labels cite block/buzz's mobile/.
# Left as they were: the safety step's drawings, the self-hosting guide's own.

